  "facts": [
    "Designed by Alfred P. Boller and erected in 1910, the Madison Avenue Bridge doubled the traffic capacity of its 1884 predecessor, becoming a key four‑lane swing bridge across the Harlem River.",
    "In 2011 the bridge handled an average of 41,423 vehicles daily, a figure that peaked at 49,487 in 2002, reflecting its vital role in New York City’s north‑south commute.",
    "During the annual New York City Marathon, runners cross this bridge on the final leg, traveling from Manhattan back to the Bronx after a brief detour through the South Bronx."
